    "https://williammary.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/WM/job/Posting-Location---William--Mary/Assistant-Professor-of-Physics_JR102162-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Physics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nJob Requisition: JR102162 Assistant Professor of Physics (Open) Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor of Physics Department: CC00105 WM001 | CDSP | Physics Dept Job Family: Faculty - Tenure Track (Less than 12 months) Worker Sub-Type: Regular (benefited) Job Requisition Primary Location: Integrated Science Center Primary Job Posting Location: Posting Location - William & Mary Job Description Summary: The Department of Physics at William & Mary, a public university of the Commonwealth of Virginia, seeks applications for a tenure track position at the Assistant Professor level. We are interested in individuals with research expertise in theoretical astroparticle physics and cosmology. Appointment will begin August 10, 2027. William & Mary values close integration of teaching and research. As an R1 university, its research spans a wide variety of areas and involves more than 20 research centers and institutes. Part of the School of Computing, Data Sciences & Physics, the Physics department offers B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. programs, has 26 full-time faculty members, more than 50 Ph.D. graduate students, and graduates approximately 40 physics major per year. More information about the department can be found at W&M-Physics. Job Description: Required Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Physics or a closely related field at the time appointment begins (August 10, 2027). Preferred Qualifications: Postdoctoral research experience. Strong research record in theoretical or computational astroparticle physics or cosmology. Ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate and graduate level and to mentor research students. Experience in the application of artificial Intelligence, machine learning and other data science techniques to research. Commitment to advance academic excellence and the success of all learners and scholars in physics. Duties include research, teaching, and service to the university. The applicant is expected to establish and maintain a vibrant, high-quality, externally funded research program that inspires a highly motivated graduate and undergraduate student body. Teaching expectation is one course per semester. Successful applicants must possess the skills to teach compelling courses in undergraduate and graduate physics and other lecture and seminar-style courses. Applicants must apply online at https://go.wm.edu/VphZB3. All applications must consist of the following materials for full consideration: Curriculum vitae; Cover letter; A statement of research interests; A statement of teaching interests; You will be prompted to submit online the names and email addresses of three references who will be contacted by the system with instructions for how to submit a letter of reference. Applicants are encouraged in their written materials to reflect on teaching and mentoring practices that advance academic excellence and the success of all learners and scholars in physics. For full consideration, submit application materials by the initial review date, 12/02/2026 Applications received after the initial review date will be considered if needed. Additional Job Description: Job Profile: JP0516 - Assistant Professor (Less than 12 months) TE - Exempt - Salary - S99 Qualifications: Compensation Grade: S99 Recruiting Start Date: 2026-10-15 Position Restrictions: Continuing E&G funded position and not term-limited EEO is the Law. Applicants can learn more about William & Mary’s status as an equal opportunity employer by viewing the \"Know Your Rights\" poster published by the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission. https:// www.eeoc.gov/know-your-rights-workplace-discrimination-illegal   Background Check: William & Mary is committed to providing a safe campus community. W&M conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Applicant Notice:   By applying for this position, you consent to William & Mary's use, review, and retention of your application materials for recruitment and employment purposes. Materials may be shared with authorized individuals participating in the hiring process and will be managed in accordance with applicable laws and university policies. Probationary Period Notice: Individuals selected for full-time staff positions will be required to complete a twelve (12) month probationary period in accordance with university policy.   Remote Work Disclaimer: Remote work eligibility is not guaranteed and is subject to approval. Employee eligibility depends on the likelihood of the employee succeeding in a remote work arrangement and the supervisor’s ability to manage remote workers. Departments and/or Human Resources may amend, alter, change, delete, or modify eligibility."
    },
    "https://williammary.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/WM/job/Posting-Location---William--Mary/Assistant-Teaching-Professor-of-Applied-Science_JR102151": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor of Applied Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nJob Requisition: JR102151 Assistant Teaching Professor of Applied Science (Open) Job Posting Title: Assistant Teaching Professor of Applied Science Department: CC00102 WM001 | CDSP | Applied Science Dept Job Family: Faculty - Non-Tenure Track (Less than 12 months) Worker Sub-Type: Fixed Term (requires end date - benefited) (Fixed Term) Job Requisition Primary Location: Integrated Science Center Primary Job Posting Location: Posting Location - William & Mary Job Description Summary: The Department of Applied Science at William & Mary, a public university of the Commonwealth of Virginia, invites applications for a 3-year, non-tenure track Assistant Teaching Professor instructional position that will begin August 10, 2027. This full-time teaching faculty appointment carries a service component commensurate with rank and comes with the possibility of ongoing renewals and a framework for promotion. We seek an individual with expertise in engineering design, additive manufacturing, advanced fabrication, prototyping, automation, instrumentation, and characterization. The successful applicant is expected to be an effective teacher and will be assigned the equivalent of a full-time teaching load, which may consist of classroom instruction, supervising student projects, and ad-hoc support of the Makerspace and its staff. Job Description: Required: Master’s degree in Engineering or a closely related field is required.    Preferred: Ph.D. or All But Dissertation (ABD) is preferred at the time appointment begins (August 10, 2027). Previous teaching experience.   Applicants must apply online at https://go.wm.edu/VphZB3 . All applications must consist of the following materials for full consideration: Curriculum vitae; Cover letter; A statement of teaching interests and experience that describes the candidate’s approach to teaching and mentoring in the context of hands-on engineering design and prototyping, which may also incorporate a discussion of how their past engineering-related work informs their current approach; A portfolio of engineering/design work and sample syllabus   Applicants are encouraged to reflect on teaching and mentoring practices that advance academic excellence and success of all learners/scholars in domains of Physics and Applied Science in any of the required documents (above).  Candidates who reach the long-list (Zoom) interview stage will be prompted to submit online the names and email addresses of three references who will be contacted by the system with instructions for how to submit a letter of reference. For full consideration, submit application materials by the initial review date, 11/30/2026. All required supplemental application materials mentioned above must be clearly identified and included with your application for full consideration. Review of applications is ongoing. Applications received after the initial review date will be considered if needed.   Information on the degree programs in the Departments of Applied Science and Physics may be found at cdsp.wm.edu.  Additional Job Description: Job Profile: JP0515 - Assistant Professor (Less than 12 months) NTE - Exempt - Salary - S99 Qualifications: Compensation Grade: S99 Recruiting Start Date: 2026-10-13 Position Restrictions: Restricted Term EEO is the Law. Applicants can learn more about William & Mary’s status as an equal opportunity employer by viewing the \"Know Your Rights\" poster published by the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission. https:// www.eeoc.gov/know-your-rights-workplace-discrimination-illegal   Background Check: William & Mary is committed to providing a safe campus community. W&M conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Applicant Notice:   By applying for this position, you consent to William & Mary's use, review, and retention of your application materials for recruitment and employment purposes. Materials may be shared with authorized individuals participating in the hiring process and will be managed in accordance with applicable laws and university policies. Probationary Period Notice: Individuals selected for full-time staff positions will be required to complete a twelve (12) month probationary period in accordance with university policy.   Remote Work Disclaimer: Remote work eligibility is not guaranteed and is subject to approval. Employee eligibility depends on the likelihood of the employee succeeding in a remote work arrangement and the supervisor’s ability to manage remote workers. Departments and/or Human Resources may amend, alter, change, delete, or modify eligibility."
    },
    "https://williammary.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/WM/job/Posting-Location---William--Mary/Professor-of-Data-Science_JR102152": {
      "title": "Professor of Data Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nJob Requisition: JR102152 Professor of Data Science (Open) Job Posting Title: Professor of Data Science Department: CC00110 WM001 | CDSP | Data Science Job Family: Faculty - Tenure Track (Less than 12 months) Worker Sub-Type: Regular (benefited) Job Requisition Primary Location: Integrated Science Center Primary Job Posting Location: Posting Location - William & Mary Job Description Summary: The Department of Data Science at William & Mary, a public university of the Commonwealth of Virginia, seeks applications for a tenured position at the Professor level in artificial intelligence, machine learning, and data-intensive research addressing large-scale computational problems with broad societal implications. Appointment will begin August 10, 2027. We are interested in individuals with research and teaching expertise in generative artificial intelligence, natural language processing, Physical AI, AI for the Physical Sciences, and related areas of artificial intelligence. Exceptional applicants from other areas of artificial intelligence will be considered. Job Description: Required Qualifications: Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in Data Science, Computer Science, or a closely related field at the time appointment begins (August 10, 2027). Previous experience in teaching and mentoring successful undergraduate and graduate research.  The successful applicant will demonstrate a track record of externally-funded research, extensive scholarly achievement, and intellectual leadership and international visibility in the broader artificial intelligence and data science research community.   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of scholarly leadership in the broader field, such as service for major conferences or journals.    Applicants must apply online at https://go.wm.edu/VphZB3 . All applications must consist of the following materials for full consideration; (Please note: No more than 5 individual documents may be uploaded into the upload field provided. Each individual file must not exceed a size limit of 5MB. If necessary, candidates can compress multiple files into a single zip file for upload): Curriculum vitae; Cover letter; A statement of teaching interests; A statement of research interests   Applicants are encouraged to reflect on teaching and mentoring practices that advance academic excellence and success of all learners/scholars in Data Science in any of the aforementioned required documents.    Candidates who reach the long-list (Zoom) interview stage will be prompted to submit online the names and email addresses of three references who will be contacted by the system with instructions for how to submit a letter of reference. Duties: Research, teaching, and service to the university. The applicant is expected to establish and maintain a vibrant externally funded and internationally recognized research program that inspires a highly motivated undergraduate student body and supports Master’s and Ph.D. students.  Teaching expectation is one course per semester. Successful applicants must possess the skills to teach compelling courses in natural language processing and other lecture and seminar-style courses, and to contribute to the development of an emergent curriculum around generative artificial intelligence.   For full consideration, submit application materials by the initial review date, 11/13/2026. Applications received after the initial review date will be considered if needed. All required supplemental application materials mentioned above must be clearly identified and included with your application for full consideration. Review of applications is ongoing. Applications received after the initial review date will be considered if needed.   Information on the degree programs in the Department of Data Science may be found at ds.wm.edu.  Additional Job Description: Job Profile: JP0519 - Professor (Less than 12 months) TE - Exempt - Salary - S99 Qualifications: Compensation Grade: S99 Recruiting Start Date: 2026-10-13 Position Restrictions: Continuing E&G funded position and not term-limited EEO is the Law. Applicants can learn more about William & Mary’s status as an equal opportunity employer by viewing the \"Know Your Rights\" poster published by the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission. https:// www.eeoc.gov/know-your-rights-workplace-discrimination-illegal   Background Check: William & Mary is committed to providing a safe campus community. W&M conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Applicant Notice:   By applying for this position, you consent to William & Mary's use, review, and retention of your application materials for recruitment and employment purposes. Materials may be shared with authorized individuals participating in the hiring process and will be managed in accordance with applicable laws and university policies. Probationary Period Notice: Individuals selected for full-time staff positions will be required to complete a twelve (12) month probationary period in accordance with university policy.   Remote Work Disclaimer: Remote work eligibility is not guaranteed and is subject to approval. Employee eligibility depends on the likelihood of the employee succeeding in a remote work arrangement and the supervisor’s ability to manage remote workers. Departments and/or Human Resources may amend, alter, change, delete, or modify eligibility."
    },
    "https://williammary.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/WM/job/Posting-Location---William--Mary/Adjunct-Professor-of-Applied-Science_JR102120": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor of Applied Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nPart time\n\nJob Requisition: JR102120 Adjunct Professor of Applied Science (Open) Job Posting Title: Adjunct Professor of Applied Science Department: CC00102 WM001 | CDSP | Applied Science Dept Job Family: Faculty - Adjunct Worker Sub-Type: Adjunct (non-benefited) Job Requisition Primary Location: Integrated Science Center Primary Job Posting Location: Posting Location - William & Mary Job Description Summary: The Department of Applied Science at William & Mary, a public university of the Commonwealth of Virginia, is recruiting a pool of qualified individuals for possible part-time adjunct teaching appointments. Beginning Spring 2027, the department anticipates instructional needs in APSC 251 Engineering Design. Within the School of Computing, Data Sciences & Physics, adjunct faculty may be responsible for: • Teaching assigned undergraduate and/or graduate courses depending on unit need • Preparing syllabi and course materials • Delivering instruction and assessing student learning • Holding office hours • Fulfilling other instructional duties consistent with departmental needs Job Description: Required Qualifications: Applicants must hold a Masters or Ph.D. in Engineering Physics, Engineering, Applied Science or a related field, or equivalent experience and qualifications. Preferred Qualifications: An M.S., Ph.D., or other appropriate terminal degree, or ABD status, in Engineering or a related field at the time of appointment (August 10 for fall or January 10 for spring). Previous academic teaching experience. Conditions of Employment: This position is also not eligible for work visa sponsorship. This is a part-time position restricted to the term to which it is assigned and hired and is not eligible for benefits. The position may require additional hours beyond the typical work week, including occasional evenings, weekends, or overnight work as needed to meet operational requirements. As part-time exempt employees, adjuncts are subject to the limitations of the Virginia Manpower Control Program. Total hours worked may not exceed an average of 29 hours per week over a twelve-month period beginning May 1 each year. Total adjunct work hours for part-time employment from May 1 through April 30 may not exceed 1,500 hours, generally equating to up to 14 credit hours for fall/spring and up to 6 for summer, not to exceed 18 credit hours for the year. Adjuncts maintain an in-person presence for the duration of their appointment.  Remote teaching opportunities are rare and subject to approval. Appointment Details: Appointments are limited to a specified term and may include the following instructional sessions: Summer Session 1: May 26 – June 26*  Summer Session 2: June 29 – July 31*  (expected contract effective date:  June 25) Summer Session 3: May 26 – July 31* Fall: August 10 – January 9 Spring: January 10 – May 24  * Summer Session Terms are subject to vary each year Applicants must apply online at https://go.wm.edu/VphZB3 . All applications must consist of the following materials for full consideration; (Please note: No more than 5 individual documents may be uploaded into the upload field provided. Each individual file must not exceed a size limit of 5MB. If necessary, candidates can compress multiple files into a single zip file for upload): Curriculum vitae; Cover letter; A statement of teaching interests; A statement of research interests; Additional materials that demonstrate experience in a Makerspace or shop for prototyping, fabricating, or other types of ‘Making’. A reference page with the contact information (including names, email addresses, and phone numbers) for three references. Applicants are encouraged to reflect on teaching and mentoring practices that advance academic excellence and success of all learners/scholars in Applied Science in any of the aforementioned required documents.  Candidates who are scheduled for interviews will be prompted to submit online the names and email addresses of three references who will be contacted by the system with instructions for how to submit a letter of reference. For full consideration, submit application materials by the initial review date, 10/28/2026. Applications received after the initial review date will be considered if needed. All required supplemental application materials mentioned above must be clearly identified and included with your application for full consideration. Review of applications is ongoing. Applications received after the initial review date will be considered if needed. Information on the degree programs in the School of Computing, Data Sciences & Physics may be found at cdsp.wm.edu. Additional Job Description: Job Profile: JP0738 - Adjunct Professor NTE - Exempt - Salary - S99 Qualifications: Compensation Grade: S99 Recruiting Start Date: 2026-09-25 Position Restrictions: Restricted Term EEO is the Law. Applicants can learn more about William & Mary’s status as an equal opportunity employer by viewing the \"Know Your Rights\" poster published by the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission. https:// www.eeoc.gov/know-your-rights-workplace-discrimination-illegal   Background Check: William & Mary is committed to providing a safe campus community. W&M conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Applicant Notice:   By applying for this position, you consent to William & Mary's use, review, and retention of your application materials for recruitment and employment purposes. Materials may be shared with authorized individuals participating in the hiring process and will be managed in accordance with applicable laws and university policies. Probationary Period Notice: Individuals selected for full-time staff positions will be required to complete a twelve (12) month probationary period in accordance with university policy.   Remote Work Disclaimer: Remote work eligibility is not guaranteed and is subject to approval. Employee eligibility depends on the likelihood of the employee succeeding in a remote work arrangement and the supervisor’s ability to manage remote workers. Departments and/or Human Resources may amend, alter, change, delete, or modify eligibility."
