    "https://williammary.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/WM/job/Posting-Location---William--Mary/Visiting-Assistant-Teaching-Professor-of-Public-Policy_JR102121": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Teaching Professor of Public Policy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nJob Requisition: JR102121 Visiting Assistant Teaching Professor of Public Policy (Open) Job Posting Title: Visiting Assistant Teaching Professor of Public Policy Department: CC00135 WM001 | CAS | Public Policy Dept Job Family: Faculty - Non-Tenure Track (12 months) Worker Sub-Type: Fixed Term (requires end date - benefited) (Fixed Term) Job Requisition Primary Location: Chancellors Hall Primary Job Posting Location: Posting Location - William & Mary Job Description Summary: The Public Policy Program at William & Mary, a public university of the Commonwealth of Virginia, invites applications for an 18 month, non-tenure track Visiting Teaching Faculty position that will begin January 10, 2027. We seek an individual with expertise in public policy to teach classes for the undergraduate public policy major (B.A. Public Policy) and for the Master’s in Public Policy (MPP) program. Exceptional candidates will have experience teaching introductory courses in public policy for undergraduates as well as upper-level courses that align with the candidate’s interests. The successful applicant will be expected to be an effective teacher and will have a [3-3] teaching load. Job Description: Required Qualifications: A Ph.D. degree (or appropriate terminal degree) in Public Policy, Economics, Government/Political Science, Law or a related field or the equivalent (master’s degree and five years working experience in public policy) is required at the time appointment begins (January 10, 2027). Applicants must have completed 18 graduate credit hours in the discipline in which they will teach. Ability to teach introductory courses in public policy for undergraduates. Ability to teach upper-level courses that align with the candidate's interests. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience in introductory courses in public policy for undergraduates. Previous experience teaching upper-level courses. Conditions of Employment: This position may require additional hours beyond the typical work week, including occasional overnight and weekend work as needed to meet the business needs of the operation.   This is a restricted position, subject to the term in which it is assigned and hired.  Applicants must apply online at https://go.wm.edu/VphZB3 . All applications must consist of the following materials for full consideration; (Please note: No more than 5 individual documents may be uploaded into the upload field provided. Each individual file must not exceed a size limit of 5MB. If necessary, candidates can compress multiple files into individual zip files for upload): Curriculum vitae; Cover letter;  A statement of teaching interests that describes your approach to teaching and mentoring and that may also incorporate a discussion of how your past scholarly work informs your approach; Unofficial graduate transcripts outlining proof of 18 graduate credit hours in the curricular area specified in the position description above. Additional forms of credit hour verification may be submitted if unofficial transcripts are not provided by your university; [optional] Other evidence of teaching effectiveness, such as course evaluations, syllabi, example assignments. Applicants are encouraged to reflect on teaching and mentoring practices that advance academic excellence and success of all learners/scholars in Public Policy in any of the aforementioned required documents. Candidates who reach the short-list (Zoom) interview stage will be prompted to submit online the names and email addresses of three references who will be contacted by the system with instructions for how to submit a letter of reference. For full consideration, submit application materials by the priority application submission deadline, October 9, 2026 . All required supplemental application materials mentioned above must be clearly identified and included with your application for full consideration. Applications received after the priority review date will be considered if needed. Review of applications is ongoing. Information on the degree programs in the Public Policy Program may be found at https://www.wm.edu/as/publicpolicy/. Benefits: William & Mary offers our full-time employees a full array of benefits including retirement, health insurance with options for expanded dental and vision along with group and optional life insurance with coverage for spouse and children, flexible spending accounts, and an EAP (Employee Assistance Program). Our employees enjoy additional university benefits such as educational assistance, professional development, wellness benefits, and a robust holiday schedule. All employees have access to fitness facilities on campus. Staff members also have access to the university libraries, and much more. To learn more, go to: https://www.wm.edu/offices/uhr/benefits/index.php?type=none Additional Job Description: Job Profile: JP0387 - Instructor (12 months) NTE - Exempt - Salary - S99 Qualifications: Compensation Grade: S99 Recruiting Start Date: 2026-09-25 Position Restrictions: Restricted Term EEO is the Law. Applicants can learn more about William & Mary’s status as an equal opportunity employer by viewing the \"Know Your Rights\" poster published by the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission. https:// www.eeoc.gov/know-your-rights-workplace-discrimination-illegal   Background Check: William & Mary is committed to providing a safe campus community. W&M conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Applicant Notice:   By applying for this position, you consent to William & Mary's use, review, and retention of your application materials for recruitment and employment purposes. Materials may be shared with authorized individuals participating in the hiring process and will be managed in accordance with applicable laws and university policies. Probationary Period Notice: Individuals selected for full-time staff positions will be required to complete a twelve (12) month probationary period in accordance with university policy.   Remote Work Disclaimer: Remote work eligibility is not guaranteed and is subject to approval. Employee eligibility depends on the likelihood of the employee succeeding in a remote work arrangement and the supervisor’s ability to manage remote workers. Departments and/or Human Resources may amend, alter, change, delete, or modify eligibility."
    },
    "https://williammary.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/WM/job/Posting-Location---William--Mary/Adjunct-Faculty---School-Psychology-and-Counselor-Education_JR102114": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - School Psychology and Counselor Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nPart time\n\nJob Requisition: JR102114 Adjunct Faculty - School Psychology and Counselor Education (Open) Job Posting Title: Adjunct Faculty - School Psychology and Counselor Education Department: CC00182 WM001 | SOE | Education Operations Job Family: Faculty - Adjunct Worker Sub-Type: Adjunct (non-benefited) Job Requisition Primary Location: School of Education Primary Job Posting Location: Posting Location - William & Mary Job Description Summary: The department of School Psychology and Counselor Education is recruiting a pool of persons for the Fall 2026, Spring 2027, and Summer 2027 semesters to be considered for possible adjunct teaching positions in our master’s and education specialist program in school psychology, our master’s degree program in counseling (clinical mental health, addictions, school counseling, and military and veterans counseling), and in our doctoral degree program in counselor education. This pool will be accessed only when an opening arises and is contingent upon funding. Your credentials will remain active as long as this pool is available. If you are still interested once this pool is closed, you must resubmit your application materials to the most current adjunct pool. Only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Hired candidates are required to provide official transcripts prior to the contracted start date. The review of applications is ongoing. Job Description: We will not sponsor applicants for work visas for this vacancy. Required Qualifications: Successful completion of a terminal degree in counselor education, school psychology, or a related field. Applicants for the MED in counseling must have a Ph.D. in Counselor Education. For those applicants for school psychology without a terminal degree, qualifications must include those enumerated in the Faculty Qualifications Manual for Alternate Methods of Qualifying Faculty to Teach. Preferred Qualifications: College teaching experience in school psychology, school counseling, counseling (e.g., clinical mental health, military veterans, relationship, marriage, and family), counselor education (Ph.D.), or related field. Position responsibilities include: Fulfill all aspects of the designated course outline. Grade assignments and exams in a timely manner. Respond to student inquiries in a timely manner. Submit final grades according to the School of Education policy.   Please indicate in your cover letter the program(s) in which you have expertise. School Psychology Counseling Counselor Education School Counseling Research Methods   Conditions of Employment: This position is restricted to a specified term. This position is not eligible for benefits. Additional Job Description: For full consideration please submit a CV, three professional references with contact information, a cover letter indicating the program(s) of interest and your qualifications to teach in the program, and an unofficial copy of your transcripts. Job Profile: JP0738 - Adjunct Professor NTE - Exempt - Salary - S99 Qualifications: Compensation Grade: S99 Recruiting Start Date: 2026-09-21 Position Restrictions: Restricted Term EEO is the Law. Applicants can learn more about William & Mary’s status as an equal opportunity employer by viewing the \"Know Your Rights\" poster published by the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission. https:// www.eeoc.gov/know-your-rights-workplace-discrimination-illegal   Background Check: William & Mary is committed to providing a safe campus community. W&M conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Applicant Notice:   By applying for this position, you consent to William & Mary's use, review, and retention of your application materials for recruitment and employment purposes. Materials may be shared with authorized individuals participating in the hiring process and will be managed in accordance with applicable laws and university policies. Probationary Period Notice: Individuals selected for full-time staff positions will be required to complete a twelve (12) month probationary period in accordance with university policy.   Remote Work Disclaimer: Remote work eligibility is not guaranteed and is subject to approval. Employee eligibility depends on the likelihood of the employee succeeding in a remote work arrangement and the supervisor’s ability to manage remote workers. Departments and/or Human Resources may amend, alter, change, delete, or modify eligibility."
    },
    "https://williammary.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/WM/job/Posting-Location---William--Mary/Adjunct-Faculty---Online-Counseling-Program_JR102115": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Online Counseling Program",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nPart time\n\nJob Requisition: JR102115 Adjunct Faculty - Online Counseling Program (Open) Job Posting Title: Adjunct Faculty - Online Counseling Program Department: CC00182 WM001 | SOE | Education Operations Job Family: Faculty - Adjunct Worker Sub-Type: Adjunct (non-benefited) Job Requisition Primary Location: School of Education Primary Job Posting Location: Posting Location - William & Mary Job Description Summary: The Department of School Psychology and Counselor Education is recruiting a pool of persons for the Fall 2026, Spring 2027, and Summer 2027 semesters to be considered for possible adjunct teaching positions in our online counseling program. This is a fully online, remote position. This pool will be accessed ONLY when an opening arises and is based on funding. Only those selected for an interview will be contacted. The review of applications is ongoing. Official transcripts will be required from candidates upon hire. Job Description: We will not sponsor applicants for work visas for this vacancy. Required Qualifications: Successful completion of a terminal degree in counselor education or related field or qualifications matching those enumerated in the Faculty Qualifications Manual for Alternate Methods of Qualifying Faculty to Teach. Preferred Qualifications: Online university teaching experience in counseling, counselor education, or related field. Position responsibilities include, but are not limited to, the following: Maintain frequent and open communication with William & Mary faculty and staff through email, mail, telephone, and any other medium deemed appropriate. Review course content, activities, and assignments prior to the term start date. Meet all designated course instruction guidelines. Provide students with timely and specific feedback. Grade assignments and exams in a timely manner based on the instructions/rubrics provided (2-3 business days). Respond to student inquiries within 1-2 business days. Monitor discussion boards and participate as applicable. Hold weekly virtual office hours for individual or group consultation. Submit final grades according to William & Mary policy and the Online Programs calendar. Submit end-of-semester feedback and reflection form. Please indicate in your cover letter the program(s) in which you have expertise. Fieldwork Clinical Mental Health Counseling Military and Veteran Counseling School Counseling Research and Assessment Methods Conditions of Employment: This position is restricted to a specified term. This position is not eligible for benefits. Additional Job Description: For full consideration please submit a CV, three professional references with contact information, a cover letter indicating the program(s) of interest and your qualifications to teach in the program, and an unofficial copy of your transcripts. Job Profile: JP0738 - Adjunct Professor NTE - Exempt - Salary - S99 Qualifications: Compensation Grade: S99 Recruiting Start Date: 2026-09-21 Position Restrictions: Restricted Term EEO is the Law. Applicants can learn more about William & Mary’s status as an equal opportunity employer by viewing the \"Know Your Rights\" poster published by the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission. https:// www.eeoc.gov/know-your-rights-workplace-discrimination-illegal   Background Check: William & Mary is committed to providing a safe campus community. W&M conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Applicant Notice:   By applying for this position, you consent to William & Mary's use, review, and retention of your application materials for recruitment and employment purposes. Materials may be shared with authorized individuals participating in the hiring process and will be managed in accordance with applicable laws and university policies. Probationary Period Notice: Individuals selected for full-time staff positions will be required to complete a twelve (12) month probationary period in accordance with university policy.   Remote Work Disclaimer: Remote work eligibility is not guaranteed and is subject to approval. Employee eligibility depends on the likelihood of the employee succeeding in a remote work arrangement and the supervisor’s ability to manage remote workers. Departments and/or Human Resources may amend, alter, change, delete, or modify eligibility."
