    "https://williammary.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/WM/job/Posting-Location---William--Mary/Associate-Teaching-Professor-of-Geology_JR102109": {
      "title": "Associate Teaching Professor of Geology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nJob Requisition: JR102109 Associate Teaching Professor of Geology (Open) Job Posting Title: Associate Teaching Professor of Geology Department: CC00101 WM001 | CAS | Geology Dept Job Family: Faculty - Non-Tenure Track (Less than 12 months) Worker Sub-Type: Fixed Term (requires end date - benefited) (Fixed Term) Job Requisition Primary Location: McGlothlin Street Hall Primary Job Posting Location: Posting Location - William & Mary Job Description Summary: The Department/Program of Geology at William & Mary, a public university of the Commonwealth of Virginia, invites applications for a 4-year, non-tenure track Associate Teaching Professor instructional position that will begin August 10, 2027. This full-time teaching faculty appointment carries a service component commensurate with rank and comes with the possibility of ongoing renewals and a framework for promotion per the Teaching Faculty Framework. We seek an individual with expertise in and enthusiasm for teaching introductory geology courses. The successful applicant will have the expertise to teach in both undergraduate lecture-based and lab-based geology courses. Additional teaching expectations will include undergraduate courses in the applicant’s area of expertise that contribute to the geology curriculum and/or general education requirements. The applicant may also contribute to our Regional Field Geology (GEOL 310), which is a field-based course that brings undergraduate students to a selected region around the world. There is no expectation of research scholarship. The successful applicant will have demonstrated a commitment to providing high-quality geology education. In practice, this will involve keeping the curricula current with the advances in the discipline and actively participating in the continuous improvement of the introductory geology curriculum. The successful applicant will be expected to be an effective teacher and will have a [3-3] teaching load. Job Description: Required Qualifications: A Master’s degree is required in Geology, Earth and Environmental Science, or a related field. Applicants must have completed 18 graduate credit hours in Geology, Earth and Environmental Science, or a related field. Ability to teach Introductory Geology and other lecture, lab, and seminar-style courses in the applicant's area of expertise that could contribute to the geology curriculum and/or general education requirements.   Preferred Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Geology, Earth and Environmental Science, or a related field or ABD is preferred at the time the appointment begins (August 10, 2027). Previous teaching experience at the introductory level. Experience developing and teaching field-based activities. Demonstrated commitment to teaching and mentoring practices that advance academic excellence and success of all learner/scholars. Conditions of Employment: This position may require additional hours beyond the typical work week, including occasional overnight and weekend work as needed to meet the business needs of the operation. Applicants must apply online at https://go.wm.edu/VphZB3 . All applications must consist of the following materials for full consideration. Please note: No more than 5 individual documents may be uploaded into the upload field provided (“i.e. Resume/Coverletter” upload field). Each individual file must not exceed a size limit of 5MB. If necessary, candidates can compress multiple files into a single zip file for upload: Curriculum vitae; Cover letter; A statement of teaching interests that describes your approach to teaching and mentoring and that may also incorporate a discussion of how your past scholarly work informs your approach; Unofficial graduate transcripts outlining proof of 18 graduate credit hours in the curricular area specified in the position description above. Additional forms of credit hour verification may be submitted if unofficial transcripts are not provided by your university;   Applicants are encouraged to reflect on teaching and mentoring practices that advance academic excellence and success of all learners/scholars in Geology in any of the aforementioned required documents. Candidates who reach the first-round virtual interview stage will be prompted to submit online the names and email addresses of three references who will be contacted by the system with instructions for how to submit a letter of reference. For full consideration, submit application materials no later than November 5, 2026 . All required supplemental application materials mentioned above must be clearly identified and included with your application for full consideration. Review of applications is ongoing. Applications received after the initial review date will be considered if needed. Information on the degree programs in the Department of Geology may be found at https://www.wm.edu/as/geology/ . Benefits: William & Mary offers our full-time employees a full array of benefits including retirement, health insurance with options for expanded dental and vision along with group and optional life insurance with coverage for spouse and children, flexible spending accounts, and an EAP (Employee Assistance Program). Our employees enjoy additional university benefits such as educational assistance, professional development, wellness benefits, and a robust holiday schedule. Housing Relocation Resources are also available to help new employees transition successfully to the area. All employees have access to fitness facilities on campus, to the university libraries, and much more. To learn more, go to: https://www.wm.edu/offices/uhr/benefits/index.php?type=none Additional Job Description: Job Profile: JP0385 - Associate Professor (Less than 12 months) NTE - Exempt - Salary - S99 Qualifications: Compensation Grade: S99 Recruiting Start Date: 2026-09-18 Position Restrictions: Restricted Term EEO is the Law. Applicants can learn more about William & Mary’s status as an equal opportunity employer by viewing the \"Know Your Rights\" poster published by the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission. https:// www.eeoc.gov/know-your-rights-workplace-discrimination-illegal   Background Check: William & Mary is committed to providing a safe campus community. W&M conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Applicant Notice:   By applying for this position, you consent to William & Mary's use, review, and retention of your application materials for recruitment and employment purposes. Materials may be shared with authorized individuals participating in the hiring process and will be managed in accordance with applicable laws and university policies. Probationary Period Notice: Individuals selected for full-time staff positions will be required to complete a twelve (12) month probationary period in accordance with university policy.   Remote Work Disclaimer: Remote work eligibility is not guaranteed and is subject to approval. Employee eligibility depends on the likelihood of the employee succeeding in a remote work arrangement and the supervisor’s ability to manage remote workers. Departments and/or Human Resources may amend, alter, change, delete, or modify eligibility."
    },
    "https://williammary.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/WM/job/Posting-Location---William--Mary/Assistant-Professor-of-Biology--Microbiology-_JR102074": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology (Microbiology)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nJob Requisition: JR102074 Assistant Professor of Biology (Microbiology) (Open) Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor of Biology (Microbiology) Department: CC00098 WM001 | CAS | Biology Dept Job Family: Faculty - Tenure Track (Less than 12 months) Worker Sub-Type: Regular (benefited) Job Requisition Primary Location: Integrated Science Center Primary Job Posting Location: Posting Location - William & Mary Job Description Summary: The Department of Biology at William & Mary, a public university of the Commonwealth of Virginia, seeks applications for a tenure track position at the Assistant Professor level in Microbiology, beginning August 10, 2027. We are interested in individuals with research and teaching expertise in microbiology with emphasis in microbial applications to biotechnology and/or biomedical sciences. Duties include research, teaching, and service to the University. The applicant is expected to establish and maintain a vibrant externally funded research program that inspires both a highly motivated undergraduate and graduate student body. Applicants should ensure that their proposed research program is well suited to a research environment in which undergraduate students serve as the primary research assistants and laboratory activities are conducted in facilities with biosafety containment levels not exceeding BSL-2. Teaching expectation is a sophomore-level microbiology course with laboratories, designed for Biology majors and appropriate for students preparing for graduate or professional schools, and another advanced course in the candidates area of expertise. Teaching expectation is 2 courses per semester. Job Description: Required Qualifications: Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in microbiology or a related field at the time appointment begins (August 10, 2027). Applicants must have completed 18 graduate credit hours in the discipline in which they will teach. Postdoctoral experience. Possess the skills to teach compelling courses in microbiology and other lecture and seminar-style courses. Ability to develop a vibrant, externally funded research program involving undergraduate and graduate students. Ability to conduct research within BSL-2 laboratory environments. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience in teaching and mentoring successful undergraduate and graduate research. Evidence of scholarly achievement or demonstrated potential as a scholar. Conditions of Employment: This position may require additional hours beyond the typical work week, including occasional overnight and weekend work as needed to meet the business needs of the operation. Applicants must apply online at https://go.wm.edu/VphZB3 . All applications must consist of the following materials for full consideration. Please note: No more than 5 individual documents may be uploaded into the upload field provided (“i.e. Resume/Coverletter” upload field). Each individual file must not exceed a size limit of 5MB. If necessary, candidates can compress multiple files into a single zip file for upload: Curriculum vitae; Cover letter; A statement of teaching interests that describes your approach to teaching and mentoring and that may also incorporate a discussion of how your past scholarly work informs your approach; A statement of research interests; Unofficial graduate transcripts outlining proof of 18 graduate credit hours in the curricular area  specified in the position description above. For international hires, a letter of graduate credit hour completion from your graduate school may be submitted if unofficial transcripts are not provided by your university. Applicants are encouraged to reflect on teaching and mentoring practices that advance academic excellence and success of all learners/scholars in microbiology in any of the aforementioned required documents. Candidates who reach the first-round virtual interview stage will be prompted to submit online the names and email addresses of three references who will be contacted by the system with instructions for how to submit a letter of reference. For full consideration, submit application materials no later than October 14, 2026. Applications received after the initial application deadline will be considered if needed. All required supplemental application materials mentioned above must be clearly identified and included with your application for full consideration. Information on the degree programs in the Department of Biology may be found at https://www.wm.edu/as/biology. Search Committee Chair Contact Shantá D. Hinton, Ph.D. She, her, hers Email: sdhinton@wm.edu Office:757-221-2587 Benefits William & Mary offers our full-time employees a full array of benefits including retirement, health insurance with options for expanded dental and vision along with group and optional life insurance with coverage for spouse and children, flexible spending accounts, and an EAP (Employee Assistance Program). Our employees enjoy additional university benefits such as educational assistance, professional development, wellness benefits, and a robust holiday schedule. Housing Relocation Resources are also available to help new employees transition successfully to the area. All employees have access to fitness facilities on campus, to the university libraries, and much more. To learn more, go to: https://www.wm.edu/offices/uhr/benefits/index.php?type=none Applicant Notice: By applying for this position, you consent to William & Mary's use, review, and retention of your application materials for recruitment and employment purposes. Materials may be shared with authorized individuals participating in the hiring process and will be managed in accordance with applicable laws and university policies. Additional Job Description: Job Profile: JP0516 - Assistant Professor (Less than 12 months) TE - Exempt - Salary - S99 Qualifications: Compensation Grade: S99 Recruiting Start Date: 2026-09-09 Position Restrictions: Continuing E&G funded position and not term-limited EEO is the Law. Applicants can learn more about William & Mary’s status as an equal opportunity employer by viewing the \"Know Your Rights\" poster published by the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission. https:// www.eeoc.gov/know-your-rights-workplace-discrimination-illegal   Background Check: William & Mary is committed to providing a safe campus community. W&M conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Applicant Notice:   By applying for this position, you consent to William & Mary's use, review, and retention of your application materials for recruitment and employment purposes. Materials may be shared with authorized individuals participating in the hiring process and will be managed in accordance with applicable laws and university policies. Probationary Period Notice: Individuals selected for full-time staff positions will be required to complete a twelve (12) month probationary period in accordance with university policy.   Remote Work Disclaimer: Remote work eligibility is not guaranteed and is subject to approval. Employee eligibility depends on the likelihood of the employee succeeding in a remote work arrangement and the supervisor’s ability to manage remote workers. Departments and/or Human Resources may amend, alter, change, delete, or modify eligibility."
    },
    "https://williammary.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/WM/job/Posting-Location---William--Mary/Associate-or-Full-Professor-of-Health-Sciences--Public-Health-_JR102098": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor of Health Sciences (Public Health)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nJob Requisition: JR102098 Associate or Full Professor of Health Sciences (Public Health) (Open) Job Posting Title: Associate or Full Professor of Health Sciences (Public Health) Department: CC00132 WM001 | CAS | Health Sciences (HSCI) Job Family: Faculty - Tenure Track (Less than 12 months) Worker Sub-Type: Regular (benefited) Job Requisition Primary Location: Adair Hall Primary Job Posting Location: Posting Location - William & Mary Job Description Summary: The Department of Health Sciences at William & Mary, a public university of the Commonwealth of Virginia, invites applications for a tenured position in Public Health at the rank of Associate or Full Professor, with an appointment beginning August 10, 2027. We seek candidates with research and teaching expertise in one or more of the following areas: biostatistics, health policy, or social and behavioral sciences. The successful applicant will be prepared to teach introductory public health courses, as well as introductory and upper-level courses in their area(s) of expertise. We seek a candidate whose teaching and research complement the strengths of the current public health faculty and contribute to or expand the department’s existing expertise, particularly in U.S. public health. Duties include research, teaching, and service to the Department and University. The applicant is expected to establish and maintain a vibrant externally funded research program that inspires a highly motivated undergraduate student body. Teaching expectation is 2 courses per semester. Successful applicants must possess the skills to teach general public health courses and other lecture and seminar-style courses, as well as contribute to mentored student research and/or experiential learning in public health. Job Description: Required Qualifications: Applicants must hold a Ph.D.  or a terminal degree in Public Health or a related field at the time the appointment begins (August 10, 2027); Applicants must have completed 18 graduate semester hours in the discipline they will be hired to teach. An established record of scholarly achievement in Biostatistics, Health Policy, or Social and Behavioral Sciences, consistent with appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Full Professor and as demonstrated through a strong publication record and contributions to the field. Evidence of the ability to establish and/or maintain a vibrant externally funded research program in Biostatistics, Health Policy, or Social and Behavioral Sciences. Demonstrated experience teaching courses in U.S. public health in both lecture and seminar formats. Demonstrated experience contributing to mentored student research and/or experiential learning in U.S. public health. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated experience directly mentoring undergraduate students in research, including supporting undergraduate research projects through completion. Evidence of teaching expertise in one or more departmental priority areas: biostatistics, health policy, or social and behavioral sciences; Demonstrated leadership in academic settings and/or Public Health practice. Conditions of Employment: This position may require additional hours beyond the typical work week, including occasional overnight and weekend work as needed to meet the business needs of the operation.  Applicants must apply online at https://go.wm.edu/VphZB3 . All applications must consist of the following materials for full consideration. Please note: No more than 5 individual documents may be uploaded into the upload field provided (“i.e. Resume/Coverletter” upload field). Each individual file must not exceed a size limit of 5MB. If necessary, candidates can compress multiple files into a single zip file for upload: Curriculum vitae; Cover letter; A statement of teaching interests that describes your approach to teaching and mentoring and that may also incorporate a discussion of how your past scholarly work informs your approach; A statement of research interests; Course evaluations from recent courses taught in biostatistics, health policy, or social and behavioral health, including both quantitative ratings and student comments, where available. Unofficial graduate transcripts outlining proof of 18 graduate credit hours in the curricular area specified in the position description above. For international hires, a letter of graduate credit hour completion from your graduate school may be submitted if unofficial transcripts are not provided by your university. Applicants are encouraged to reflect on teaching and mentoring practices that advance academic excellence and success of all learners/scholars in Health Sciences in any of the aforementioned required documents. Candidates who reach the first-round virtual interview stage will be prompted to submit online the names and email addresses of three references who will be contacted by the system with instructions for how to submit a letter of reference. For full consideration, submit application materials no later than October 18, 2026 . Applications received after the initial application deadline will be considered if needed. All required supplemental application materials mentioned above must be clearly identified and included with your application for full consideration. Information on the degree programs in the Department of Health Sciences may be found at https://www.wm.edu/as/health-sciences/ . Benefits William & Mary offers our full-time employees a full array of benefits including retirement, health insurance with options for expanded dental and vision along with group and optional life insurance with coverage for spouse and children, flexible spending accounts, and an EAP (Employee Assistance Program). Our employees enjoy additional university benefits such as educational assistance, professional development, wellness benefits, and a robust holiday schedule. Housing Relocation Resources are also available to help new employees transition successfully to the area. All employees have access to fitness facilities on campus, to the university libraries, and much more. To learn more, go to: https://www.wm.edu/offices/uhr/benefits/index.php?type=none Additional Job Description: Job Profile: JP0517 - Associate Professor (Less than 12 months) TE - Exempt - Salary - S99 Qualifications: Compensation Grade: S99 Recruiting Start Date: 2026-09-17 Position Restrictions: Continuing E&G funded position and not term-limited EEO is the Law. Applicants can learn more about William & Mary’s status as an equal opportunity employer by viewing the \"Know Your Rights\" poster published by the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission. https:// www.eeoc.gov/know-your-rights-workplace-discrimination-illegal   Background Check: William & Mary is committed to providing a safe campus community. W&M conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Applicant Notice:   By applying for this position, you consent to William & Mary's use, review, and retention of your application materials for recruitment and employment purposes. Materials may be shared with authorized individuals participating in the hiring process and will be managed in accordance with applicable laws and university policies. Probationary Period Notice: Individuals selected for full-time staff positions will be required to complete a twelve (12) month probationary period in accordance with university policy.   Remote Work Disclaimer: Remote work eligibility is not guaranteed and is subject to approval. Employee eligibility depends on the likelihood of the employee succeeding in a remote work arrangement and the supervisor’s ability to manage remote workers. Departments and/or Human Resources may amend, alter, change, delete, or modify eligibility."
    },
    "https://williammary.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/WM/job/Posting-Location---William--Mary/Assistant-Professor-of-Biology--Ecologist-_JR102072": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology (Ecologist)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nJob Requisition: JR102072 Assistant Professor of Biology (Ecologist) (Open) Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor of Biology (Ecologist) Department: CC00098 WM001 | CAS | Biology Dept Job Family: Faculty - Tenure Track (Less than 12 months) Worker Sub-Type: Regular (benefited) Job Requisition Primary Location: Integrated Science Center Primary Job Posting Location: Posting Location - William & Mary Job Description Summary: The Department of Biology at William & Mary, a public university of the Commonwealth of Virginia, seeks applications for a tenure track position at the Assistant Professor level in Ecology. Appointment will begin August 10, 2027. We are interested in individuals with research and teaching expertise in ecology with a specialization in biostatistics and/or quantitative biology. Applicants whose research is focused on any aspect of ecology will be considered as long as there is a strong quantitative aspect to their research and teaching interests. Duties include research, teaching, and service to the University. The applicant is expected to establish and maintain a vibrant externally funded research program that inspires a highly motivated body of undergraduate and master’s students. Teaching duties include a large, undergraduate introductory biostatistics course that serves students across the biology department, engaging undergraduate courses in ecology, and other lecture or seminar-style courses in the applicant’s area of expertise, including advanced or graduate-level biostatistics course. Teaching expectation is 2 courses per semester. Job Description: Required Qualifications : Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in biology, biomathematics or biostatistics, or a closely related field, at the time appointment begins (August 10, 2027). Applicants must have completed 18 graduate credit hours in the discipline in which they will teach Evidence of research expertise in ecology, biomathematics, or significant experience in other areas of quantitative ecology. Evidence of teaching expertise in ecology, biostatistics, or significant experience in other areas of quantitative biology or biomathematics. Ability to teach compelling courses in ecology and biostatistics. Experience (or ability) to teach other lecture and seminar-style courses. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience in ecology and an established record of mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate research. Evidence of scholarly achievement, including peer-reviewed publications in competitive outlets and nationally competitive grants or other awards. Postdoctoral research experience is strongly preferred. A research program that can leverage on-campus and local natural resources and sites will be viewed as desirable.  Conditions of Employment: This position may require additional hours beyond the typical work week, including occasional overnight and weekend work as needed to meet the business needs of the operation.     Applicants must apply online at https://go.wm.edu/VphZB3 . All applications must consist of the following materials for full consideration. Please note: No more than 5 individual documents may be uploaded into the upload field provided (“i.e. Resume/Coverletter” upload field). Each individual file must not exceed a size limit of 5MB. If necessary, candidates can compress multiple files into a single zip file for upload:  Curriculum vitae;  Cover letter; A 2-3 page statement of teaching interests that describes your approach to teaching and mentoring and that may also incorporate a discussion of how your past scholarly work informs your approach   A 2-3 page statement of research interests; Unofficial graduate transcripts outlining proof of 18 graduate credit hours in the curricular area specified in the position description above. For international hires, a letter of graduate credit hour completion from your graduate school may be submitted if unofficial transcripts are not provided by your university    Applicants are encouraged to reflect on teaching and mentoring practices that advance academic excellence and success of all learners/scholars in any of the aforementioned required documents.      Candidates who reach the first-round virtual interview stage will be prompted to submit online the names and email addresses of three references who will be contacted by the system with instructions for how to submit a letter of reference.    For full consideration, submit application materials no later than October 17, 2026 . Applications received after the initial application deadline will be considered if needed. All required supplemental application materials mentioned above must be clearly identified and included with your application for full consideration.     Information on the degree programs in the Department of Biology may be found at https://www.wm.edu/as/biology/ . Please contact Dr. Dan Cristol ( dacris@wm.edu ) with any questions regarding the position.       Benefits  William & Mary offers our full-time employees a full array of benefits including retirement, health insurance with options for expanded dental and vision along with group and optional life insurance with coverage for spouse and children, flexible spending accounts, and an EAP (Employee Assistance Program).     Our employees enjoy additional university benefits such as educational assistance, professional development, wellness benefits, and a robust holiday schedule. Housing Relocation Resources are also available to help new employees transition successfully to the area. All employees have access to fitness facilities on campus, to the university libraries, and much more. To learn more, go to: https://www.wm.edu/offices/uhr/benefits/index.php?type=none    Additional Job Description: Job Profile: JP0516 - Assistant Professor (Less than 12 months) TE - Exempt - Salary - S99 Qualifications: Compensation Grade: S99 Recruiting Start Date: 2026-09-09 Position Restrictions: Continuing E&G funded position and not term-limited EEO is the Law. Applicants can learn more about William & Mary’s status as an equal opportunity employer by viewing the \"Know Your Rights\" poster published by the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission. https:// www.eeoc.gov/know-your-rights-workplace-discrimination-illegal   Background Check: William & Mary is committed to providing a safe campus community. W&M conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Applicant Notice:   By applying for this position, you consent to William & Mary's use, review, and retention of your application materials for recruitment and employment purposes. Materials may be shared with authorized individuals participating in the hiring process and will be managed in accordance with applicable laws and university policies. Probationary Period Notice: Individuals selected for full-time staff positions will be required to complete a twelve (12) month probationary period in accordance with university policy.   Remote Work Disclaimer: Remote work eligibility is not guaranteed and is subject to approval. Employee eligibility depends on the likelihood of the employee succeeding in a remote work arrangement and the supervisor’s ability to manage remote workers. Departments and/or Human Resources may amend, alter, change, delete, or modify eligibility."
    },
    "https://williammary.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/WM/job/Posting-Location---William--Mary/Assistant-Professor-of-Modern-African-American-History_JR102091": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Modern African American History",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nJob Requisition: JR102091 Assistant Professor of Modern African American History (Open) Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor of Modern African American History Department: CC00094 WM001 | CAS | History Dept Job Family: Faculty - Tenure Track (Less than 12 months) Worker Sub-Type: Regular (benefited) Job Requisition Primary Location: James Blair Hall Primary Job Posting Location: Posting Location - William & Mary Job Description Summary: The Harrison Ruffin Tyler Department of History at William & Mary, a public university of the Commonwealth of Virginia, seeks applications for a tenure track position at the Assistant Professor level in modern African American history. Appointment will begin August 10, 2027. Duties include research, teaching, and service to the University. The applicant is expected to establish and maintain a vibrant research program that inspires a highly motivated undergraduate student body, as well as Master’s and Ph.D. students. Teaching expectation is 2 courses per semester. Successful applicants must possess the skills to teach compelling courses in African American history and other lecture and seminar-style courses, and to contribute to the graduate program. Job Description: Required Qualifications : A Ph.D. in History or a related field at the time appointment begins (August 10, 2027). Completion of 18 graduate credit hours in the discipline in which they will teach. Research experience in modern African American history. Experience teaching (or ability to teach) courses in African American history and other lecture and seminar-style courses. Experience mentoring graduate students or ability to contribute to the graduate program. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience in teaching and mentoring successful undergraduate research. Evidence of scholarly achievement or demonstrated potential as a scholar. Conditions of Employment: This position may require additional hours beyond the