    "https://williammary.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/WM/job/Posting-Location---William--Mary/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate-of-Physics--Condensed-Matter-Theory-_JR101950": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate of Physics (Condensed Matter Theory)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-23\nFull time\n\nJob Requisition: JR101950 Postdoctoral Research Associate of Physics (Condensed Matter Theory) (Open) Job Posting Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate of Physics (Condensed Matter Theory) Department: CC00105 WM001 | CDSP | Physics Dept Job Family: Faculty - Postdoctoral Research Associate (12 months) Worker Sub-Type: Fixed Term (requires end date - benefited) (Fixed Term) Job Requisition Primary Location: Small Hall Primary Job Posting Location: Posting Location - William & Mary Job Description Summary: The Department of Physics at William & Mary, a public university of the Commonwealth of Virginia, invites applications for a postdoctoral research associate position, expected to begin on August 10, 2027. Earlier start dates may be possible depending on availability. We seek an individual with expertise in theoretical quantum matter to join Daniele Guerci’s research group. Information on Dr. Guerci's research group can be found here: https://danieleguerci.github.io/ The initial appointment is for one year, with the possibility of a second year based on performance and funding availability. Job Description: Required Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Physics, or related field, at the time appointment begins (expected to begin August 10, 2027). Preferred Qualifications: Experience in analytical and/or computational modeling of interacting electron systems. Current research topics include, but are not limited to, unconventional superconductivity, fractionalization, and electronic crystallization in quantum materials. Applicants must apply online at https://www.wm.edu/offices/uhr/careers/ . For full consideration, please upload your curriculum-vitae, cover letter, and research statement. Candidates who reach the long-list (Zoom) interview stage will be prompted to submit online the names and email addresses of three references who will be contacted by the system with instructions for how to submit a letter of reference. For full consideration, submit application materials by the review begin date, February 19th 2027. Applications received after the review date will be considered if needed. Information on the Department of Physics may be found at www.wm.edu/as/physics . Posting Range: $65,000-$70,000, commensurate with experience and internal alignment Additional Job Description: Job Profile: JP0518 - Postdoctoral Research Associate (12 months) - Exempt - Salary - S99 Qualifications: Compensation Grade: S99 Recruiting Start Date: 2026-07-23 Position Restrictions: Restricted Funds & Restricted Term EEO is the Law.  Applicants can learn more about William & Mary’s status as an equal opportunity employer by viewing the \"Know Your Rights\" poster published by the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission. https:// www.eeoc.gov/know-your-rights-workplace-discrimination-illegal   Background Check: William & Mary is committed to providing a safe campus community. W&M conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check.    Remote Work Disclaimer: Remote work eligibility is not guaranteed and is subject to approval. Employee eligibility depends on the likelihood of the employee succeeding in a remote work arrangement and the supervisor’s ability to manage remote workers. Departments and/or Human Resources may amend, alter, change, delete, or modify eligibility."
    },
    "https://williammary.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/WM/job/Posting-Location---William--Mary/Postdoctoral-Fellow-of-Computer-Science--Robust-and-Adaptive-Intelligence-_JR101939": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow of Computer Science (Robust and Adaptive Intelligence)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-23\nFull time\n\nJob Requisition: JR101939 Postdoctoral Fellow of Computer Science (Robust and Adaptive Intelligence) (Open) Job Posting Title: Postdoctoral Fellow of Computer Science (Robust and Adaptive Intelligence) Department: CC00100 WM001 | CDSP | Computer Science Dept Job Family: Faculty - Postdoctoral Research Associate (12 months) Worker Sub-Type: Fixed Term (requires end date - benefited) (Fixed Term) Job Requisition Primary Location: Integrated Science Center Primary Job Posting Location: Posting Location - William & Mary Job Description Summary: The Department of Computer Science at William & Mary, a public university of the Commonwealth of Virginia, invites applications for a postdoctoral fellow position in the Robust and Adaptive Intelligence Laboratory, expected to begin September 10, 2026. We seek an individual to contribute to two intertwined threads of research: (i) AI-based approaches for routing under uncertainty, including dynamic dispatch and stochastic and online vehicle routing at scale; and (ii) explainability of AI-based sequential decision-making, combining formal logic, large language models, and planning so that decisions produced by complex systems can be understood, audited, and trusted. The appointed researcher will publish in top venues in artificial intelligence, machine learning, and operations research; contribute to open-source releases; and work closely with graduate students in the lab. The initial appointment is for one year, with the possibility of renewal based on performance and funding availability. Job Description: Required Qualifications: Applicant must hold a Ph.D. in Computer Science, or a related field, at the time appointment begins (expected to begin September 10, 2026). Preferred Qualifications: Experience in Sequential Decision-Making under Uncertainty, Planning, and Machine Learning. Strong software-engineering skills and a track record of publishing at top AI/ML/OR venues or of deploying research systems in real-world settings are welcome. Applicants must apply online at https://www.wm.edu/offices/uhr/careers/ . Submit a curriculum vitae, a cover letter, two names for letters of references, and a statement of research. For full consideration, submit application materials by the review begin date: August 10, 2026 . Applications received after the review date will be considered if needed. Information on the Department of Computer Science may be found at https://cdsp.wm.edu/computerscience/ . Posting Range: $70,000 - $75,000, commensurate with experience and internal alignment Additional Job Description: Job Profile: JP0518 - Postdoctoral Research Associate (12 months) - Exempt - Salary - S99 Qualifications: Compensation Grade: S99 Recruiting Start Date: 2026-07-21 Position Restrictions: Restricted Funds & Restricted Term EEO is the Law.  Applicants can learn more about William & Mary’s status as an equal opportunity employer by viewing the \"Know Your Rights\" poster published by the U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission. https:// www.eeoc.gov/know-your-rights-workplace-discrimination-illegal   Background Check: William & Mary is committed to providing a safe campus community. W&M conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check.    Remote Work Disclaimer: Remote work eligibility is not guaranteed and is subject to approval. Employee eligibility depends on the likelihood of the employee succeeding in a remote work arrangement and the supervisor’s ability to manage remote workers. Departments and/or Human Resources may amend, alter, change, delete, or modify eligibility."
